      "content": "That is correct. In a 2-mark question like this, each character identified correctly earns you one mark. \n\n**Model Answer for Exam:**\n> Gertrude and Mrs Lithebe. (2)\n\n---\n### 📖 Concept & Thought Process (How to Understand It):\n* **The Concept / Rule:** Comprehension questions require you to identify specific referents (pronouns or nouns) within the text. You must ensure you capture the full scope of the reference.\n* **The Thought Process (How to Unpack It):**\n  1. *Step 1 — Locate:* Find the line mentioned (line 4).\n  2. *Step 2 — Identify:* Look at the sentence preceding the pronoun 'them' to see who is being discussed or acted upon.\n  3. *Step 3 — Verify:* Check if the pronoun is plural; if it is, your answer must account for all individuals involved in that specific action.\n* **How DBE Markers Score It:**\n  * **Mark 1:** Identifying Gertrude.\n  * **Mark 2:** Identifying Mrs Lithebe.\n  * *Note:* If you only name one, you lose half the marks. If you name an incorrect character, you lose that specific mark.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** When a question asks 'To whom', always check if the pronoun is plural. If it is, look for a pair or a group. Never leave an answer ambiguous—be specific with names as they appear in the text."
    }
